WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:03.614
("Blue Danube Waltz" by Johann Strauss II)

00:00:03.614 --> 00:00:04.447
(snip, snip)

00:00:04.447 --> 00:00:07.221
(snip, snip)

00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:11.214
(trimmer starts and revs)

00:00:11.214 --> 00:00:13.797
(click, click)

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.570
- [Narrator] Welcome to
Powis Castle and Garden.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.750
Once home to a Welsh prince,
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.603
now home to the biggest hedges in the UK.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.750
They're around 400 years old,

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.070
and it's this guys job to cut them.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:41.950
- My name's Dan Bull ,and
I'm the gardener here

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.890
at Powis Castle and Garden.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.730
The larch hedges were
planted in the 18th century,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.020
and the fashion changed
in the Victorian era,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.868
and that's the unique shape we have today.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.250
(upbeat music)

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.940
We have 14 larch stumps on the terraces,

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:56.880
and the big hedge,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.470
that's approximately 8,000
square meters of hedging.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.770
The box hedges and the formal hedging

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:05.410
is about 7,000 square meters.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.630
So in total, we have 15,000
square meters of hedges to cut.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.623
And one being 55 feet tall.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:14.520
- [Narrator] For anyone
who doesn't like heights,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.210
might be best you look away now.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.570
- [Dan] One of the highlights for me

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.354
is when we get the cherry pickers in,

00:01:20.354 --> 00:01:22.890
and spending the time
floating around the sky

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.890
looking at the wildlife
and cutting the hedges.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.250
Fortunately, I quite like heights

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.370
so it's lovely being up there.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.250
- [Narrator] Back in
the day it took 10 men

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.490
four months to trim all the hedges,

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:36.310
tying ladders together
and using hand shears.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.050
Nowadays, Dan's able to
complete the mammoth task

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.050
in just eight weeks.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.670
- With mechanization,
we've been able to use

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.100
electric and petrol hedge
cutters, long-reach hedge cutters.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.176
It's a lot better than trying
to do it with a scythe.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.430
(gentle music)

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.530
- [Narrator] Along with the hedges,

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.040
Dan is among the seven gardeners

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.350
who work throughout the
year, come rain or shine,

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.590
to manage the ever evolving grounds.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.720
- [Dan] I do a bit of everything.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.700
Rather than being just stuck
in one part of the garden.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.080
I've been here for 12 years.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:05.920
I love coming to work.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.120
I'm quite lucky in my role.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.610
I get here early most mornings

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.300
and take my dog round the garden,

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.133
so it's lovely.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.530
I'll be here at seven
o'clock in the morning,

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:15.160
the mists rising, and
you're just looking over

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.890
at the castle and the garden,

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.140
and feel quite privileged
to be working here.

